<article class="env-definition" id="02T1">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02T1">Definition <span data-tag="02T1">115.23.7</span>.</a> Let $(S, \delta )$ be as in Chow Homology, Situation <a href="/tag/02QL" data-tag="02QL">42.7.1</a>. Let $X$ be locally of finite type over $S$. Assume $X$ integral and $\dim _\delta (X) = n$. Let $D_1, D_2$ be two effective Cartier divisors in $X$. Let $Z \subset X$ be an integral closed subscheme with $\dim _\delta (Z) = n - 1$. The <em>$\epsilon $-invariant</em> of this situation is </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \epsilon _ Z(D_1, D_2) = n_ Z \cdot m_ Z  \]
</div>
  <p> where $n_ Z$, resp. $m_ Z$ is the coefficient of $Z$ in the $(n - 1)$-cycle $[D_1]_{n - 1}$, resp. $[D_2]_{n - 1}$. </p>
</article>